This example shows how to use the KCW code with the 2D Coulomb cutoff
(assume_isolated='2D', Sohier et al., PRB 96, 075448 (2017)) to compute the
KI band structure of a h-BN monolayer. The layer lies in the x-y plane; the
cell height is c = 6a (~15 A). The steps are:

1) scf calculation with the 2D cutoff on the full 3x3x1 grid, with enough
   empty bands for the Wannierization of the empty manifold.
   input=hBN.scf.in, output=hBN.scf.out

2) dielectric tensor of the same cell with ph.x (epsil=.true.), from a
   separate non-magnetic scf (2D cutoff, 6x6x1). The tensor is written to
   eps.dat, which kcw.x reads from the run directory. Only its in-plane block
   is used: alpha_2D = (eps_par - 1) c / (4 pi).
   input=hBN.scf_eps.in, hBN.ph.in   output=hBN.scf_eps.out, hBN.ph.out, eps.dat

3) Wannierization of the occupied manifold (N sp2 + N pz), results in ./wann_occ.
   The Wannier-interpolated bands along G-M-K-G are in wann_occ/hBN_band.dat.

4) Wannierization of the empty manifold (B pz + N s), results in ./wann_emp.
   The 2D cutoff shifts all eigenvalues, so the disentanglement windows are set
   relative to the lowest unoccupied level of step 1. The Wannier-interpolated
   bands along G-M-K-G are in wann_emp/hBN_emp_band.dat.

5) interface to KCW, with the 2D cutoff
   input=hBN.kcw-wann2kcw.in, output=hBN.kcw-wann2kcw.out

6) screening coefficients, with the 2D cutoff and l_vcut=.true.: the q+G=0
   terms are computed with the 2D scheme (charged-sheet term + 2D
   Gygi-Baldereschi, screened with eps(q) = 1 + r0 q, r0 = 2 pi alpha_2D).
   With the 2D cutoff and l_vcut=.true., eps.dat is required.
   input=hBN.kcw-screen.in, output=hBN.kcw-screen.out

7) KI Hamiltonian, interpolation and band structure along G-M-K-G, with the
   2D cutoff and l_vcut=.true. Only the on-site (R=0, i=j) KI corrections are
   used (on_site_only=.true.), and the screening parameters are corrected beyond
   second order (l_alpha_corr=.true.), as in the koopmans workflow.
   input=hBN.kcw-ham.in, output=hBN.kcw-ham.out

The KI band structure is in hBN.kcw_bands.dat.

Notes
- assume_isolated='2D' must be used consistently in pw.x and in all kcw.x
  steps: kcw.x stops if it differs from the value in the pw.x data.
- The 2D cutoff requires mp3 = 1.
- The q+G=0 terms can also be added a posteriori: run the screening with
  l_vcut=.false., then calculation='cc' with l_vcut=.true. (same mp1-mp3,
  outdir and eps.dat), and add the printed "uPi(q+G=0) estimation" and
  "rPi(q+G=0) estimation" to the unrelaxed and relaxed Pi of each orbital.
- The parameters (ecutwfc = 40 Ry, 3x3x1 mesh) are chosen to keep the example
  fast. They are not converged.
